/**
 * Sprint 18R — Decision Support + Clarification Architecture Review: corpus.
 *
 * This is a design-architecture corpus, distinct from both the golden vocabulary-calibration
 * corpus (`conversational-brain-golden-intents.ts`) and the Sprint 17R general_pm_advice boundary
 * corpus (`conversational-brain-general-pm-advice-boundary-cases.ts`). Its purpose is narrower and
 * more forward-looking than either: it records, for realistic PMFreak PM phrasing, (a) which of two
 * *not-yet-built* architecture pieces — a `decision_support` production handler, or a real
 * `needs_clarification` response strategy — a message should eventually route to, and (b) what the
 * *current, safe, already-shipped* system does with that same message today (`currentSafeMappedIntent`,
 * per the Sprint 10R adapter's documented `decision_support -> unsupported` /
 * `needs_clarification -> general_pm_advice` mapping decisions).
 *
 * `desiredFutureRoute`, `currentSafeMappedIntent`, `targetKind`, `riskLevel`, `requiresNewHandler`,
 * `requiresClarification`, and `shouldExecuteAction` are all policy decisions recorded at authoring
 * time (mirroring the Sprint 17R boundary corpus's `policyTarget`/`shouldCurrentSystemHandle`
 * pattern) — they describe where a message *should* eventually route and what it requires
 * architecturally, not necessarily what today's classifiers actually output for it right now. Some
 * cases were deliberately phrased to collide with an existing category's vocabulary (see each
 * `architectureCategory`'s "_vs_X" naming) specifically to document where that collision already
 * happens live — see `rationale`/`notes` for cases where the live classifiers were checked against
 * this exact input while authoring the corpus.
 *
 * `shouldExecuteAction` is `false` for every case in this corpus — this sprint does not execute any
 * action, real or simulated, for any input.
 */

